ensus-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+07:07/60:00 c36/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_q5riyf3i","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && grep -r \"TODO\\|FIXME\" . --include=\"*.el\" --include=\"*.org\" --include=\"*.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -20 > /tmp/todo.txt"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:22:06] \n[t+07:21/60:00 c37/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_3ub2rxwt","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/tmp/todo.txt"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:22:11] ./emacs.d/test/test-file-guard.el:TODO.md and IDEAS.md are freely writable.\"\n./emacs.d/test/test-file-guard.el:    ;; TODO.md and IDEAS.md are freely writable\n./emacs.d/test/test-file-guard.el:                 \"/root/personalization/audit/iar/darwin/TODO.md\"))\n./emacs.d/elpa/gptel-20260826.2228/gptel-anthropic.el:                ;; TODO(tool) handle this error better\n./emacs.d/elpa/gptel-20260826.2228/gptel-anthropic.el:                (error (pop (plist-get info :tool-use)))) ;TODO: nreverse :tool-use list\n./emacs.d/elpa/gptel-20260826.2228/gptel-anthropic.el:   ;; TODO(tool) can :text be :null?\n./emacs.d/elpa/gptel-20260826.2228/gptel-anth