ensus-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+04:20/60:00 c30/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_giiezex1","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/failure-reduction/census-updates.log"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[census-update] continuo census-window output for 2026-09-12:\n== census-window: agent=continuo day=2026-09-12 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n--- runs (start UTC | timeout? turns tools exit fate):\nSep 12 00:07:25 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=30, exit=0 \nSep 12 00:29:26 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=21, exit=0 \nSep 12 00:46:59 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=15, exit=0 \nSep 12 01:00:19 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=6, exit=1 \nSep 12 01:20:53 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=30, exit=0 \nSep 12 01:35:19 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=34, exit=0 \nSep 12 02:03:23 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=19, exit=1 \nSep 12 02:19:59 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=18, exit=0 \nSep 12 02:35:16 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=37, exit=0 \nSep 12 02:57:39 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=60, exit=0 \nSep 12 03:31:45 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=27, exit=1 \nSep 12 04:22:34 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=37, exit=0 \nSep 12 04:34:10 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=29, exit=0 \nSep 12 04:47:14 | to=0 | turns=0, tools=47, exit=0 \nSep 12 05:35:36 | to=0 | tu