; when a same-tool call's args score below 0.5 token-set Jaccard against the previous same-tool call's args, the chain counter resets -- the iterator keeps its monotone count, the investigator gets its counter wiped. One-char tokens dropped before comparison (the changing counter is noise, the shape is the signal); empty token sets conservative (never reset on unparseable args). Calibrated by measurement: tail -N vs tail -M = 1.0, git-log paging = 0.67, ssh-vs-curl = 0.07, same-host different-command = 0.5-0.7 (borderline; a genuinely different next command breaks the chain one step later, so the count self-corrects). Threshold defcustom in configs/loop-guard.el with unit-float :safe predicate; defensive fallback read in the guard. Differential-verified: OLD code fails 3 new tests (investigation walk blocked at 10; reset-then-rechain; similarity boundary), NEW code passes all 16 chain tests + full suite 997/997 (was 991, +6: convergence reset, iterator still blocks, git-log paging still blocks, reset-then-rechain, identical-run-then-iterator, similarity boundary). The 489-round-trip iterator contract stays pinned.\n44da3c9 loop-guard-chain hook-order fix: add-hook prepends by default, so the chain guard registered BEFORE the identical-args guard. run-hook-with-args-until-success short-circuits at first non-nil return, so once the chain guard blocked at the soft threshold, the identical guard never ran for that call, the call never entered history, and the chain count recomputed from the same frozen history every retry -- frozen at exactly \"10 times\", hard stop unreachable, model could retry forever (observed live 2026-09-03 06:26-06:28: ~50 soft blocks, zero escalation). Fix: APPEND registration (t), load-bearing-order comments. Tests: bridge escalation walk (25 calls must block AND stop through the real bridge) + hook-order pin. Differential-verified: old order fails both new tests, new order passes. Suite 988/988.\n098fb63 loop guard v2: chain detection -- same-tool chains with varying args\n\n[t+05:46/60:00 c29/300]"}]
