[2026-09-19 10:50:43] REQ 260919104701-32 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=64 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_xlzxy5ss","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/i.ar/README.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[10:50:24] # i.ar\n\nA self-modifying AI operating environment built in Emacs, running in a hardened Podman container, powered by local LLMs via Ollama. No cloud. No telemetry. No backdoors.\n\n* Quickstart\n\n** Prerequisites\n- Podman (container runtime)\n- Emacs 28+ (for local development without container)\n- Ollama running on a reachable host (local or WireGuard mesh)\n- A personalization repository (see below)\n\n** Clone\n\n#+begin_src bash\n# Just want to use the tool (no personalization submodule):\ngit clone https://github.com/randazzo-ignacio/i.ar.git\n\n# Want to work on i.ar or understand the codebase (includes personalization submodule):\ngit clone --recursive https://github.com/randazzo-ignacio/i.ar.git\n#+end_src\n\nThe =personalization/= submodule contains knowledge bases, per-agent tasks, and audit logs. Users should create their own personalization repo with their own knowledge and agent configurations. See =personalization/= for the default setup.\n\n** Build\n\n#+begin_src bash\ncd i.ar\n./containers/build.sh\n#+end_src\n\n** Run\n\nThere is one entry point: =iar.sh=. It has two modes -- interactive (default) and loop (=--loop=).\n\nBoth modes require =--personalization= pointing to a directory with =knowledge/=, =tasks/=, and =audit/= subdirectories.\n\n*** Interactive Sessions (default mode)\n\nDrops you into an Emacs gptel chat buffer with an agent loaded. You're the conductor -- you type, the agent responds, you direct the work.\n\n#+begin_src bash\n# Interactive session with self-modification (for development with darwin)\n./utils/iar.sh \\\n  --self-modification \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --gptel-fork ~/repos/gptel\n\n# Interactive session (no self-modification, load agents via C-c a inside Emacs)\n./utils/iar.sh \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --gptel-fork ~/repos/gptel\n#+end_src\n\n*** Autonomous Loops (=--loop=)\n\nRuns an agent for N cycles with cooldown between each. Sends Telegram notifications if =AGENT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN= and =AGENT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID= are set. Container names are auto-suffixed with PID so multiple loops can run in parallel without collisions.\n\n#+begin_src bash\n# Darwin autonomous loop (code changes, self-modification enabled)\n./utils/iar.sh --loop \\\n  --self-modification \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --agent darwin \\\n  --gptel-fork ~/repos/gptel \\\n  --max-cycles 50\n\n# Gardener autonomous loop (prompt refinement, no self-modification)\n./utils/iar.sh --loop \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --agent gardener \\\n  --gptel-fork ~/repos/gptel \\\n  --max-cycles 10\n\n# Playground loop on GPU model (sophon, 120B, 128K context)\n./utils/iar.sh --loop \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --agent playground \\\n  --model nemotron-3-super:120b \\\n  --ctx 131072 \\\n  --ollama-host 10.66.0.5:11434 \\\n  --max-cycles 999 \\\n  --cooldown 300\n\n# Playground loop on CPU model (daftpunk, 30B, 128K context)\n./utils/iar.sh --loop \\\n  --personalization ~/repos/iar-personalization \\\n  --agent playground \\\n  --model granite4.1:30b \\\n  --ctx 131072 \\\n  --ollama-host 10.66.0.3:11434 \\\n  --max-cycles 999 \\\n  --cooldown 300\n#+end_src\n\n*** Model and Host Selection\n\nThe =--model= and =--ctx= flags control which LLM runs and how much context window it gets. These are critical for local models -- the KV cache scales linearly with context size, so a 120B model at 1M context would need ~320GB of RAM just for the cache.\n\n| Flag | Default | Description |\n|------+---------+-------------|\n| =--model NAME= | =glm-5.2:cloud= | Model name (must be in =metaconfig/gptel.el= model list) |\n| =--ctx N= | =1048576= (1M) | Max context window in...[+4916 chars]
