op-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el has a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el fails due to missing iar--current-project-name (need to load iar-agent-utils.el) (test-loop-chain.el)\n* [2026-09-18 03:27:15] Fixed test-loop-chain.el: added proper test environment setup (IAR_PROJECT, paths, require iar-agent-utils) to avoid usage log warning about iar--current-project-name being void.\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el has a syntax error in the let-binding for fork-path (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Fixed lexical-binding warning in test-loop-chain.el, test suite passes (16/16). (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n* 2026-09-18 -- Fixed lexical-binding warnings in test files (13 files) to eliminate test suite warnings.\n- [2026-09-18] Test suite for iar-loop-guard-chain.el now passes (16/16) and lexical-binding warnings fixed. (emacs.d/test/test-loop-chain.el)\n- [2026-09-18] Read token burn audit: confirmed one runaway cycle caused 42% of burn; batch-read law is key. (knowledge/aria/token-burn-audit.md)\n2026-09-18: test-loop-chain.el passes (16/16). Census window for 2026-09-18 shows 6 exit1 runs (truncated-output guard firing as designed).\n- [2026-09-19] Checked census window for continuo (00:00-06:30 UTC window in progress, no journald lines yet) (census-window.sh)\n[2026-09-19] Noticed test suite scripts use tail/head for small data (elpa dirs). No batch-read law violations in agent code observed during wander.\n- [2026-09-19] Census window script for continuo failed when run via ssh (path: /var/home/nacho/repos/iar-personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh) - investigate.\n- [2026-09-19] Investigated census window script failure: script exists and works when called with correct arguments (date then agent). The earlier failure was due to argument order. (census-window.sh)\n\n[t+03:48/60:00